diff --git a/DESIGN.md b/DESIGN.md
index 5c6cd9a..3a8d6ff 100644
--- a/DESIGN.md
+++ b/DESIGN.md
@@ -21,3 +21,11 @@ CHG-060 public static SEO pages reuse AppShell, BrandHeader, InfoFooter and fixe
 Owner-approved: `/` opens the real trainer, informational and setup URLs are flat, and every built-in sequence has a distinct path. Retain marketing as `MarketingOverview` inside About with the existing brand, routine, free/local promise, CTA and mode guide cards. Public About/Contact/manuals use the same actual app components and fixed navigation as their in-app equivalents. Preserve the original marketing capture as historical evidence. No rebrand or unrelated layout changes. Review changed About/public captures in both pinned browsers and preserve unrelated baselines; original performance budgets apply.
 
 Existing native selects remain OS-owned: practice delay/start-source, appearance, History progress filter and private preview simulation. Native popup geometry is intentionally platform-dependent; no authored dropdown redesign is authorized by this routing change. Preserve existing labels, keyboard behavior and numeric validation contracts. This explicit ownership decision also applies to the retained native template adapters.
+
+
+## CHG-062 — shared information icons
+
+The app header owns About, @ Contact, Settings in this order. BrandHeader owns the shared 24px outlined SVGs (1.8 stroke), 44px controls, focus/tooltips/current state and responsive geometry. All share theme text, existing orange current/focus accent and a theme-aware hover surface. No font glyph for @; no duplicate footer links. Footer disclosure/copyright/divider and fixed bottom navigation stay. Runtime values live in BrandHeader.css; no independent page overrides.
+
+
+CHG-062 performance correction under review: the in-app Settings control retains its existing native button action (with shared icon styling, accessible name/current state and guarded route callback); About and Contact are real links. Static editorial/public link-mode shells retain a real Settings href. This preserves the released Settings keyboard/action contract rather than requiring identical HTML tags for different control purposes. Visual references remain unchanged; complete acceptance is still required.
